-- title:
--   Torus-shell averages are values of cyclic smooth vectors
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be a finite place of $\mathbb{Q}$ (a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$), let $W : \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v) \to \mathbb{C}$ be a function admitting an open subgroup $U_v \le \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ with $W(gk) = W(g)$ for all $k \in U_v$ and all $g$, let $\varpi$ be an element of the valuation ring whose image in $\mathbb{Q}_v$ is nonzero and of valuation $\exp(-1)$, and let $b \in \mathbb{N}$. The assertion is: for every $g_3 \in \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$, every $k_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$, every homomorphism $\eta : \mathbb{Q}_v^\times \to \mathbb{C}^\times$, every $c \in \mathbb{N}$ such that $\eta$ is trivial on the $c$-th higher unit group at $v$ while for each $m < c$ some element of the $m$-th higher unit group has $\eta(u) \neq 1$, with $c \le b$, and every Haar measure $\mu_2$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ (for the Borel structures attached to $v$), put for $n = (n_1,n_2) \in \mathbb{Z}^2$
--   $$A(n) = \int_{|u|=1} \Bigl(\int_{K_1(\mathfrak{p}^b)} W\bigl(\iota(\varpi^{n_2}I_2 \cdot \mathrm{diag}(\varpi^{n_1}u,1) \cdot k_0k)\, g_3\bigr)\, d\mu_2(k)\Bigr)\eta(u)\, d\mu^\times(u),$$
--   where $K_1(\mathfrak{p}^b)$ is the pullback to $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ of the adelic level-one subgroup of level $v^b$, $\iota$ is the upper-left embedding $\mathrm{GL}_2 \hookrightarrow \mathrm{GL}_3$ fixing the last coordinate, and $\mu^\times$ is the measure on units obtained by comapping along $u \mapsto u$ the multiplicative measure $|x|^{-1}$ times the self-dual additive Haar measure at $v$; and let $A^\vee(n)$ be the same expression with $W(\,\cdot\, g_3)$ replaced by its dual $x \mapsto W(w_3\,{}^{t}x^{-1} g_3)$ ($w_3$ the long Weyl element) and with $k$ replaced by ${}^{t}(k^{-1})$. Then there exist $\Phi$ in the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the right translates of $W$, and $\Phi^\vee$ in the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the right translates of $x \mapsto W(w_3\,{}^{t}x^{-1} g_3)$, each invariant on the right under some open subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$, such that for all $n \in \mathbb{Z}^2$ one has $A(n) = \Phi\bigl(\iota(\varpi^{n_2}I_2\cdot\mathrm{diag}(\varpi^{n_1},1))\bigr) = \Phi(\mathrm{diag}(\varpi^{n_1+n_2},\varpi^{n_2},1))$ and likewise $A^\vee(n) = \Phi^\vee(\mathrm{diag}(\varpi^{n_1+n_2},\varpi^{n_2},1))$.
--
--   This identifies the level-$\mathfrak{p}^b$ averaged, $\eta$-twisted shell integrals of a smooth function on $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$, and of its Weyl-dual, as the values along the diagonal torus of single smooth vectors in the cyclic subspaces generated by those functions. It serves as an input to [`LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_rational_torusShellAverage_and_dual_of_admissible_of_isGL3PsiWhittakerFn`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_rational_torusShellAverage_and_dual_of_admissible_of_isGL3PsiWhittakerFn), where asymptotics of such torus arrays are deduced from admissibility.
